<section class="sp-hero"><div class="sp-hero-i pxw"><img data-px=".14" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784382265423-d5b445f04405?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&h=1200&q=75" alt="rows of colourful spices displayed in bowls" width="1800" height="1200" fetchpriority="high"></div><div class="sp-dust" aria-hidden="true"><i style="--x:8%;--d:0s;--s:6px;--t:9s"></i><i style="--x:18%;--d:2s;--s:4px;--t:11s"></i><i style="--x:27%;--d:4s;--s:8px;--t:13s"></i><i style="--x:39%;--d:1s;--s:5px;--t:10s"></i><i style="--x:48%;--d:3s;--s:7px;--t:12s"></i><i style="--x:57%;--d:5s;--s:4px;--t:9s"></i><i style="--x:66%;--d:2.5s;--s:6px;--t:14s"></i><i style="--x:74%;--d:0.5s;--s:9px;--t:11s"></i><i style="--x:83%;--d:3.5s;--s:5px;--t:10s"></i><i style="--x:92%;--d:1.5s;--s:7px;--t:13s"></i><i style="--x:34%;--d:6s;--s:4px;--t:12s"></i><i style="--x:71%;--d:7s;--s:6px;--t:10s"></i></div><div class="sp-w sp-hero-t"><p class="sp-ey">A guide to the spice shelf</p><h1><span>Warmth,</span> <span>colour</span> <span>&amp; aroma</span></h1><p class="sp-hero-p">Spicery is an independent guide to cooking with spices: how to buy them, wake them up and blend them into something your own.</p><div class="sp-hero-a"><a class="sp-btn" href="#atlas">Open the spice atlas</a><a class="sp-ln" href="tempering-guide.html">The art of tempering &rarr;</a></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-in"><div class="sp-w sp-in-g"><div class="sp-in-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784382265435-9820bd9cd1bc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=900&q=75" alt="colourful spices and dried flowers displayed in bowls" width="700" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div><p class="sp-ey">First, a secret</p><p class="sp-big rv">Most of a spice&rsquo;s flavour lives in its oils. Heat and a little fat <em>wake them up</em>; time and light put them back to sleep.</p><div class="sp-in-n stg"><div class="rv"><b data-count="30">30</b><small>sec</small><span>to toast whole seeds in a dry pan</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="6">6</b><small>mo</small><span>ground spices stay lively, roughly</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="2">2</b><small>yrs</small><span>whole spices keep their character</span></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-at" id="atlas"><div class="sp-w sp-at-g"><div><p class="sp-ey">The spice atlas</p><h2 class="rv">Eight spices, one wheel</h2><p class="sp-p">Tap a spice to see how it tastes, when to add it and what it loves to be cooked with.</p><div class="sp-at-o" id="at-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div><div class="sp-at-w"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" id="at-svg" role="group" aria-label="Spice wheel"></svg></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-cards"><div class="sp-w"><p class="sp-ey">From market to jar</p><h2 class="rv">Four rules for fresh spices</h2><div class="sp-stack"><div class="sp-card" style="--i:0"><div class="sp-card-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1781728924364-341245a93766?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=520&q=75" alt="sacks filled with colourful spices at a market" width="720" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="sp-card-t"><span>01 / 04</span><h3>The market</h3><p>Buy where spices sell fast. Turnover is the best guarantee of freshness.</p></div></div><div class="sp-card" style="--i:1"><div class="sp-card-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1686596572519-4cbc1c47ddcb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=520&q=75" alt="bags filled with different coloured spices" width="720" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="sp-card-t"><span>02 / 04</span><h3>The colour</h3><p>Bright colour and strong aroma mean the oils are still there.</p></div></div><div class="sp-card" style="--i:2"><div class="sp-card-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758745464235-ccb8c1253074?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=520&q=75" alt="colourful spices and dried goods on display" width="720" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="sp-card-t"><span>03 / 04</span><h3>The choice</h3><p>Buy whole where you can, and in small amounts you will use in months.</p></div></div><div class="sp-card" style="--i:3"><div class="sp-card-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633881614907-8587c9b93c2f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=520&q=75" alt="a plate with whole spices and nuts" width="720" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="sp-card-t"><span>04 / 04</span><h3>The kitchen</h3><p>At home, keep them dark, dry and cool, in airtight jars.</p></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-tm" id="tempering"><div class="sp-w sp-tm-g"><div class="sp-tm-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 260" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="170" cy="200" rx="150" ry="34" fill="#3A2A20"/><path d="M20 160q150 110 300 0" fill="#2A1E17" stroke="#5A4232" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M318 166 L350 150" stroke="#5A4232" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/><ellipse cx="170" cy="168" rx="128" ry="20" id="tm-oil" fill="#C99A3B" opacity=".25"/><g id="tm-seeds"></g><g id="tm-steam" opacity="0"><path d="M120 120q-10-20 0-40t0-40" class="stm"/><path d="M170 110q-10-20 0-40t0-40" class="stm"/><path d="M220 120q-10-20 0-40t0-40" class="stm"/></g></svg><div class="sp-tm-ph rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768729340375-5ca3544635d8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=680&h=420&q=75" alt="a woman grinding spices in a stone mortar" width="680" height="420" loading="lazy"></div></div><div><p class="sp-ey">Watch it bloom</p><h2 class="rv">Temper, step by step</h2><p class="sp-p">Tempering, called tadka or chhaunk in India, blooms whole spices in hot fat and pours their flavour over a dish. Press start and follow along.</p><ol class="sp-tm-l" id="tm-l"><li>Heat two tablespoons of oil or ghee</li><li>Add mustard seeds; wait for them to pop</li><li>Add cumin seeds; let them sizzle and darken slightly</li><li>Add dried chilli and curry leaves, then pour</li></ol><button type="button" class="sp-btn" id="tm-go">Start tempering</button><p class="sp-tm-o" id="tm-o" aria-live="polite">The pan is cold.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="sp-s sp-bl" id="blend"><div class="sp-w"><div class="sp-cen"><p class="sp-ey">The blend builder</p><h2 class="rv">Mix your own house blend</h2><p class="sp-p">Set the parts of each spice and watch the jar fill. We will tell you what your blend leans towards.</p></div><div class="sp-bl-g rv"><div class="sp-bl-s" id="bl-s"></div><div class="sp-bl-j"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 280" aria-hidden="true"><defs><clipPath id="jar"><path d="M40 70h120v170q0 24-24 24H64q-24 0-24-24z"/></clipPath></defs><rect x="52" y="30" width="96" height="34" rx="6" fill="#5A4232"/><g clip-path="url(#jar)" id="bl-layers"></g><path d="M40 70h120v170q0 24-24 24H64q-24 0-24-24z" fill="none" stroke="#F5EBDD" stroke-opacity=".5" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M58 90v130" stroke="#fff" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><p class="sp-bl-o" id="bl-o" aria-live="polite"></p></div></div></div></section>

